.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Exception: connectors module ships production runtime deps (yaml, cockatiel,
# nanoid; ~2.2 MB) committed so /plugin install + /plugin update both deliver
# a fully-working stack without npm install. See connectors/.gitignore for
# the full rationale.
!marketplace/plugin/connectors/node_modules/
!marketplace/plugin/connectors/node_modules/**

# Python bytecode. lib/ gained an importable module (org_import.py) and a test
# suite, so running either now leaves __pycache__ directories in the tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Signing material. NEVER commit: the Developer ID private key IS the identity,
# and the App Store Connect .p8 authorises notarization submissions.
# These live in ~/.sutra-signing (mode 600), outside the repo, on purpose.
*.p8
*.p12
*.certSigningRequest

# Per-session governance markers and ledgers, written by the plugin's own
# hooks on every tool call (flow-gate, dispatch-gate, placement, marker-lib).
# Per-machine runtime state, regenerated on demand, and never read from git:
# org_api's _read_jsonl_tail returns (0, [], False) for a missing ledger, and
# every test that touches these paths builds its own sandbox with a synthetic
# session id (mktemp + CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR), so none reads the repo's copies.
#
# NOTE: files already tracked under these paths STAY tracked -- .gitignore
# does not untrack. These rules only stop NEW artifacts from accumulating.
.claude/sessions/
.claude/flow-inner
#
# Per-turn ledgers written by marketplace/plugin/runtime/ledger.sh on every
# tool call: <proj>/.sutra/turn/<session>/<turn>.jsonl, its flat twin, and the
# `current` turn-id pointer (no .jsonl suffix, by design -- ledger.sh:185
# exempts it from the retention roll-off so the live turn is never swept).
# Same class as .claude/sessions/ above: per-machine runtime state, rolled off
# on its own retention, never read from git -- no file under these paths has
# ever been tracked. The `**/` prefix matters: a nested project dir gets its
# own .sutra/ (marketplace/plugin/sutra-ui/), so a root-anchored rule misses it
# -- which is also why creation-stop-check.sh:22, whose input is
# `git status --porcelain -uall`, kept flagging the nested `current` pointer as
# an unclassified new artifact. Ignoring it at source settles both.
**/.sutra/turn/
**/.enforcement/flow-journal/
**/.enforcement/atom-gate.jsonl
**/.enforcement/dispatch-gate.jsonl
**/.enforcement/marker-contamination.jsonl
**/.enforcement/pytest-isolation-guard.jsonl
**/.enforcement/placement/gate-log.jsonl

# ...and the per-turn markers and ledgers the SAME hooks rewrite constantly.
# These were tracked from the 2026-08-02 import onward and have been churning
# in every commit since -- 16 files of machine state in a diff whose subject
# was one .gitignore line. Untracked 2026-09-15 (git rm --cached; the files
# stay on disk). Safe because nothing reads them from git: every hook that
# uses one creates it (mkdir -p / touch / >>) and guards for its absence
# ([ -f ]), so a fresh clone rebuilds them on the first tool call.
# Per-session and per-machine local state, same class as the markers below.
# heartbeats/ is one file per session id written by the session hook;
# placement-mode and settings.local.json are this machine's own choices;
# .enforcement/placement/ holds the placement engine's per-run ledgers
# (compliant-turns, gate-log.jsonl, touch-log.jsonl, touch-errors.log) --
# the last two were already enumerated individually below, and the whole
# directory is local state, so the directory rule replaces the guesswork.
# None is read from git: every hook that uses one creates it and guards for
# its absence, so a fresh clone rebuilds them on the first tool call.
.claude/heartbeats/
.claude/placement-mode
.claude/settings.local.json
.enforcement/placement/

.claude/depth-registered
.claude/flow-classified
.claude/flow-type-resolved
.claude/input-routed
.claude/placement-registered
.claude/sutra-estimation.log
**/.enforcement/.estimation-last-ts
**/.enforcement/clock-skew-sidecar.jsonl
**/.enforcement/d30-policy-only.log
**/.enforcement/marker-resets.jsonl
**/.enforcement/phase-exit-audit.jsonl
**/.enforcement/build-layer-ledger.jsonl
**/.enforcement/flow-gate.jsonl
**/holding/state/prompts/

# Per-run ledgers the hooks keep adding NEW names for. Enumerated, not
# wildcarded, and that is deliberate: .enforcement/ still holds 8 tracked
# files (cascade, md-standard, routing-misses, test-gate, rtk-gate,
# compliant-turns, the push receipt) and .claude/ holds 43 including
# commands/ and hooks/, so `**/.enforcement/` would shadow real content.
# This list will need extending again when a hook invents another name.
**/.enforcement/bash-summary.jsonl
**/.enforcement/proto*-warnings.log
**/.enforcement/placement/touch-log.jsonl
**/.enforcement/placement/touch-errors.log
**/.enforcement/permission-gate.jsonl

# ...and the extension this list predicted, with the collision it warned
# about. completion-protocol.jsonl exists TWICE: the repo-root copy is one
# of the 8 tracked files named above, while the sutra-ui copy is per-run
# telemetry the plugin hook appends to. So this one rule is PATH-SPECIFIC,
# not `**/` -- the wildcard would name the tracked ledger too. (An ignore
# rule cannot untrack what is already in the index, so nothing breaks today;
# it would bite the day the root copy is removed and re-added, silently.)
# permission-gate.jsonl has no tracked twin anywhere, so it takes the
# ordinary `**/` form above.
marketplace/plugin/sutra-ui/.enforcement/completion-protocol.jsonl
**/.sutra/creation-guard.jsonl

# A LOCAL REPRO FIXTURE, not a shipped file. It drives a real mission into
# the founder"s own store (--live) to hold a check_met=false window open for
# inspection, and it writes a `shadow.enabled` settings fixture -- which the
# accessor lint in test_shadow_flag.py rightly flags on any tracked file that
# is not named test_*. It stays on disk and still runs; it simply is not part
# of the release.
marketplace/plugin/sutra-ui/repro-unmet-is-not-needs-you.py

# SHADOW MISSION OUTPUT, not repo content. The delegate workdir IS
# marketplace/plugin/sutra-ui, so a task told to "create a file called X"
# writes X here and it shows up as untracked. These two are artifacts of
# acceptance missions run on 2026-09-17.
#
# IGNORED RATHER THAN DELETED on purpose: mission m-56e8a6ee4f1f is PAUSED
# with a file_exists probe on "Joy Stefan", so removing the file would make a
# live mission's check fail the moment it resumes. Ignoring keeps it off the
# release and leaves the probe answerable.
marketplace/plugin/sutra-ui/Joy Stefan
marketplace/plugin/sutra-ui/Joy Tadanki
